     (a) Use, copy, modify, and distribute the Software;
     (b) Create, build, inspect, modify, distribute, and publish Packages;
     (c) Execute Packages on any infrastructure you control;
     (d) Create derivative works of the Software;
     (e) Sublicense the above rights to others under the same terms.

3. Managed Service Restriction

   You may NOT use the Software to provide a Managed Service without a
   separate commercial license from Schift. Contact licensing@schift.io
   for commercial licensing.

   This restriction applies only to offering Package execution as a
   service to third parties. It does not restrict any other use of the
   Software, including internal use, local execution, self-hosted
   execution, development, testing, or distribution.

4. Format Specification

   The .apm container format (byte layout, content-hash algorithm,
   manifest schema, and capability vocabulary as defined in SPEC.md)
   is an open specification. Anyone may implement readers, writers,
   validators, or runners that consume or produce .apm files without
   any license from Schift, provided they do not use Schift's
   copyrighted source code to do so in violation of Section 3.

   For the avoidance of doubt: building your own .apm-compatible tools
   from scratch, or building a runner that executes .apm packages for
   your own use or your organization's use, does not require a
   commercial license.

